                        </latex-image>
                    </image>
                </figure>
                <p>
                    <ol marker="(a)">
                        <li>
                            <p>Count the squares that lie wholly inside the outline of the leaf.</p>
                            <solution component="lesson-plan"><p><m>14</m> for the leaf in the figure. Learners' own leaves give their own counts.</p></solution>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>Count the squares that the outline passes through.</p>
                            <solution component="lesson-plan"><p><m>23</m> for the leaf in the figure.</p></solution>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>Some of the squares in part (b) are almost full and some are almost empty. What single number could each of them count as?</p>
                            <solution component="lesson-plan"><p>About <m>\tfrac{1}{2}</m>: on average such a square is about half covered, so the nearly full ones and the nearly empty ones balance.</p></solution>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>Estimate the area of the leaf as (number in part (a)) <m>+ \tfrac{1}{2} \times</m> (number in part (b)) square centimetres.</p>
                            <solution component="lesson-plan"><p><m>14 + \tfrac{1}{2} \times 23 = 14 + 11.5 = 25.5\,\text{cm}^2</m>.</p></solution>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>Repeat parts (a), (b) and (d) on the grid of 0.5 cm squares below. Each small square has area <m>0.5 \times 0.5 = 0.25\,\text{cm}^2</m>.</p>
                            <figure xml:id="fig-leaf-on-fine-grid">
                                <caption>The same leaf on 0.5 cm squares.</caption>
                                <image width="60%">
                                    <shortdescription>The same leaf on 0.5 cm squares: 78 small squares wholly inside, about 50 cut by the edge.</shortdescription>
